# Working instructions for this project, kept out of the published repository.
# They are notes to whoever (or whatever) is building it, not documentation for
# anyone reading the source. What a contributor needs is in README.md.
CLAUDE.md

# Key material, which never belongs in this repository.
#
# Test certificates live on the machine that is building the app and nowhere
# else. A .p12 carries a private key; committing one publishes it, and a public
# AGPL repository is the worst possible place for that to happen. The rule is
# the extension rather than the filename, so a new test file is covered before
# anyone remembers to add it.
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.pem
*.key

# Documents used for testing, which live in the project root.
#
# A signed PDF carries the signer's certificate in the clear — name, email
# address and personal identifier included — so committing one publishes them.
# Anchored to the root so the committed fixtures under app/src stay tracked:
# those are deliberate, and signed by throwaway keys.
/*.pdf

# And documents dropped in the root to try something out. A signature image is
# somebody's signature; a .svg of one in a public repository is that signature
# published. Anchored to the root so app/public/favicon.svg and the bundled
# assets stay tracked.
/*.svg
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
